  "title": "Prayer at Taq Kasra — Mada'in",
  "data": "At Taq Kasra, the ruins of Khosrow's palace, pray two or more units of prayer, as Imam Ali (a.s.) prayed there.\nAt the ruins, recite [Surah Ad-Dukhan](A48), verses 25-29, as Imam Ali (a.s.) taught:\nكَمْ تَرَكُوْا مِنْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّعُيُوْنٍۙ‏(25)\nKAM TARAKOO MIN JANNAATINW WA O’OYOONINW.\nHow many gardens and springs did they leave behind!\nوَّزُرُوْعٍ وَّمَقَامٍ كَرِيْمٍۙ‏(26)\nWA ZOROO-I’NW WA MAQAAMIN KAREEMINW.\nFields and splendid places,\nوَّنَعْمَةٍ كَانُوْا فِيْهَا فٰكِهِيْنَۙ‏(27)\nWA NA’MATIN KAANOO FEEHAA FAAKEHEENA.\nand the affluence wherein they rejoiced!\nكَذٰلِكَ‌ وَاَوْرَثْنٰهَا قَوْمًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‏(28)\nKAZAALEK, WA AWRASNAAHAA QAWMAN AAKHEREEN.\nSo it was; and We bequeathed them to another people.\nفَمَا بَكَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ السَّمَآءُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَا كَانُوْا مُنْظَرِيْنَ‏(29)\nFAMAA BAKAT A’LAYHEMUS SAMAAA-O WAL ARZO WA MAA KAANOO MUNZAREEN.\nSo neither the sky wept for them, nor the earth; nor were they granted any respite.\nImam Ali (a.s.) then added:\nاِنَّ هٰؤُلَاۤءِ كَانُوْا وَارِثِيْنَ فَاَصْبَحُوْا مَوْرُوْثِيْنَ\nINNA HAA'ULAA'I KAANOO WAARITHEENA FA-ASBAHOO MAWROOTHEEN\nThese people were inheritors, then they became the inherited.\nلَمْ يَشْكُرُوا النِّعْمَةَ فَسُلِبُوْا دُنْيَاهُمْ بِالْمَعْصِيَةِ\nLAM YASHKURUN NI'MATA FASULIBOO DUNYAAHUM BIL MA'SIYAH\nThey were not grateful for the blessing, so they were stripped of their world for their disobedience.\nاِيَّاكُمْ وَكُفْرَ النِّعَمِ لَا تَحِلُّ بِكُمُ النِّقَمُ\nIYYAAKUM WA KUFRAN NI'AMI LAA TAHILLU BIKUMUN NIQAM\nBeware of ingratitude for blessings, lest punishments befall you.",
  "merits": "Praying at Taq Kasra, the remains of the palace of the Sasanian king Khosrow I at al-Mada'in, is recommended because Imam Ali (a.s.) offered a prayer there.\n\n'Ammar al-Sabati reports that when Imam Ali (a.s.) came to al-Mada'in with Dalaf ibn Bujayr, he went into the courtyard of Khosrow's palace and prayed there. Then he rose and asked Dalaf, with whom was a group from the people of Sabat, to come with him. The Imam (a.s.) went round the chambers of Khosrow, and at every place he told Dalaf what had been there. Dalaf would answer, \"By Allah, it is just as you say.\" When he had gone round the whole palace, Dalaf said to him, \"O my master and chief, it is as if you had put these things in their places yourself!\"\n\nIt is also reported that when Imam Ali (a.s.) passed by the ruins of Khosrow's palace at al-Mada'in, a man with him recited this verse of poetry: \"Winds blew over the traces of their homes, as if they had kept an appointment.\" The Imam (a.s.) said he should rather have recited these verses of [Surah Ad-Dukhan](A48), and then added his own words, both given here."
}
